<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francis Farewell</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1793–1829</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francis Farewell was a former British naval officer who in 1824 led a small party of traders from the Cape to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durban">Port Natal</a>, founding the settlement that became Durban. He visited Shaka, who granted the traders land around the bay, and he traded for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> court. Farewell was killed on a journey in 1829.</p></div>
